From c0d5a5589e92f02720976d17d5966ae1a98a97b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giang Nguyen <33104857+giang17@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:53:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Copy the WIC pixels into bitmaps created from a WIC
 source with the TARGET option too.

CreateBitmapFromWicBitmap() skipped the CopyPixels() step for bitmaps created
with D2D1_BITMAP_OPTIONS_TARGET since 3bf270c39a0, so such a target started out
transparent instead of holding the WIC source's pixels.  That skip was a
hypothesis from the Serum 2 tooltip investigation which the investigation itself
refuted (the tooltip layers came from the image brush ignoring source_rect), and
its claim about Windows has no source: the documented behaviour is that the
bitmap is created by copying the WIC bitmap, whatever the options are.

Cubase 15 depends on the copy.  It composes its skin images in several passes
over one WIC bitmap: create a target from the WIC bitmap, draw one layer into
it, read it back into the same WIC bitmap through CopyFromBitmap() and Map(),
and repeat for the next layer.  With every pass starting from zero only the last
layer survived; the MixConsole level meter images ended up with 99 of 2013
pixels set and the meters stayed empty (issue 338).  Restoring the copy makes
them appear.
---
 dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c | 18 +++++-------------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c b/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
index 4ed9d8265c73..5066c69a7990 100644
--- a/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
@@ -792,19 +792,11 @@ HRESULT d2d_bitmap_create_from_wic_bitmap(struct d2d_device_context *context, IW
     rect.Y = 0;
     rect.Width = size.width;
     rect.Height = size.height;
-    /* Skip CopyPixels for TARGET bitmaps — they should start transparent (zeroed).
-     * On Windows, CreateBitmapFromWicBitmap with D2D1_BITMAP_OPTIONS_TARGET ignores
-     * the WIC source data. Without this skip, the WIC bitmap retains GPU readback
-     * content from previous frames, causing alpha accumulation on semi-transparent
-     * regions (e.g. tooltip rounded-rect corners rendered via SOURCE_OVER). */
-    if (!(bitmap_desc.bitmapOptions & D2D1_BITMAP_OPTIONS_TARGET))
-    {
-        if (FAILED(hr = IWICBitmapSource_CopyPixels(bitmap_source, &rect, pitch, data_size, data)))
-        {
-            WARN("Failed to copy bitmap pixels, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
-            free(data);
-            return hr;
-        }
+    if (FAILED(hr = IWICBitmapSource_CopyPixels(bitmap_source, &rect, pitch, data_size, data)))
+    {
+        WARN("Failed to copy bitmap pixels, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
+        free(data);
+        return hr;
     }
 
     hr = d2d_bitmap_create(context, size, data, pitch, &bitmap_desc, bitmap);
